{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.BnMtcAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.BnMtcAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Endomorphism"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.bnAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.bnAction","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/bn-mtc-action.lean#L79-L119","doc":"**The braid representation does not factor through `S_n`**\n(`prop:bn-mtc-action`).\n\nLet `C` be braided monoidal and let `V` be an object on which the\nbraiding is non-symmetric — the defining property of a simple in an\nobservable MTC (`def:observable-mtc`, field\n`braiding_nonsymmetric`), supplied here as `hV` because a\ncontent-block sibling cannot import a sibling.\n\nLet `π : B →* S` be any quotient sending the braid generator `σ` to\nan involution — this is exactly `B_n ↠ S_n`, under which `σ_i` maps\nto the transposition `(i, i+1)`.\n\nThen no representation `ρ` sending `σ` to the braiding factors\nthrough `π`.  This is the `.md` claim; it is *derived* from `hV`\nrather than projected out of it.\n\n**Scope, stated so it is not overread.**  This is the statement at\nthe `V ⊗ V` level — equivalently `n = 2`, where the `.md`'s\n`ρ_n(σ_i)` is the bare braiding.  The general-`n` form quantifies\nover `Aut (V^{⊗ n})` with `ρ_n(σ_i) = id^{⊗(i-1)} ⊗ c_{V,V} ⊗\nid^{⊗(n-i-1)}`, and needs the tensor-power construction plus the\nfact that whiskering an automorphism preserves \"square ≠ 1\"; that\nis not built here.  The obstruction argument itself is already\ngeneral: `not_factorsThrough_of_sq_ne_one` is stated for arbitrary\ngroups and consumes only `ρ σ ^ 2 ≠ 1`, so extending to general `n`\nis supplying that hypothesis for the whiskered braiding, not\nredoing the argument.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:bn-mtc-action}`\nRef: [kitaev2006] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aop.2005.10.005\nRef: [moore-seiberg1989] https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01238857 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:bn-mtc-action","label":"prop:bn-mtc-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/bn-mtc-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braiding_sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braiding_sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/bn-mtc-action.lean#L65-L77","doc":"A non-symmetric braiding on `V` is an element of `Aut (V ⊗ V)`\nwhose square is not the identity.  This is the bridge from the\ncategorical statement `c ∘ c ≠ id` to the group statement\n`x ^ 2 ≠ 1` that `not_factorsThrough_of_sq_ne_one` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_factorsThrough_of_sq_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_factorsThrough_of_sq_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/bn-mtc-action.lean#L46-L63","doc":"**No factorisation through a quotient that kills the generator's\norder.**\n\nIf `π : B →* S` sends `σ` to an element squaring to `1`, while\n`ρ : B →* G` sends `σ` to an element whose square is not `1`, then\n`ρ` cannot be written as `φ ∘ π`.\n\nThis is the group-theoretic content of the proposition, stated\nwithout reference to braids: `π` is `B_n ↠ S_n`, `σ` is a braid\ngenerator `σ_i` (whose image is a transposition, hence an\ninvolution), and `ρ` is the categorical representation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}